flowchart TD

    %% PUBLIC DISCOVERY (Phase A/B — no sign-in required)
    A[Visitor: Browse public venues and events on /explore]
    B{Find by address or find by event}
    C[Record DB: Return active venues / upcoming events with facility names]
    D[Visitor: Open event detail page - description, times, venue, live capacity]

    A --> B --> C --> D

    %% SIGN-IN GATE (Google OAuth2 - first login auto-registers the member)
    E{Signed in?}
    F[Site: Redirect through Google OAuth - invited role applied on first login]
    G[Member: Signed in with local role]

    D --> E
    E -->|No| F --> G
    E -->|Yes| G

    %% REGISTRATION FLOW (Phase C)
    H[Member: Request to join event]
    I{Guards}
    J[409: already registered]
    K[409: event at capacity - derived from venue's facility max_capacity]

    G --> H --> I
    I -->|pass| L[Record DB: Create active schedule row at the event's venue]
    I -->|fail| J
    I -->|fail| K

    %% POST-SIGNUP SELF SERVICE (Phases C/D/E)
    M[Member: See registration in My Schedule and download iCal]
    N[Member: Fill and submit facility signup form - view answers or export PDF]
    O[Staff: Send one-way message - member reads it in Profile > My Messages]

    L --> M
    M --> N
    M --> O

    P[Site: Toast confirmation - counts refresh publicly]

    L --> P
